{
  "format": "forge.chat_agent/v1",
  "id": "ca_servicedesk",
  "name": "Northwind service desk (tool-mode intake example)",
  "description": "A service desk that files people's requests to three teams' intakes, used as tools: shared fields (email, department, manager, cost center, needed by) are asked once, requests are kept for the person across conversations, and submitting one opens a ticket (open-ticket.workflow.json).",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "agent",
      "kind": "agent",
      "name": "Service desk",
      "outputs": [
        "tools",
        "agents"
      ],
      "config": {
        "description": "Northwind's service desk.",
        "instruction": "You're Northwind's service desk: one place to ask the company's teams for things. Be friendly and brief.\n\nThe teams' intakes are your tools. When someone needs something, start a request to each team that does it, together when they need several, with what they've already told you. Then ask what the requests still need, a few related questions at a time: what several requests share (their email, department, manager, cost center, when they need it) is asked once.\n\nWhen the requests are ready, read each back as a table (present) and ask if it's right. When they say yes, submit them: each opens a ticket with its team, which the chat shows. Give them the ticket numbers once they're in.\n\nIf they ask about a request from before, list theirs; an open one can be picked up here. Questions about the company you can't answer: say which team to ask.",
        "model": {
          "provider": "",
          "name": ""
        },
        "thinking_level": "",
        "max_output_tokens": null,
        "ask_person": false,
        "state_schema": {}
      }
    },
